The `else` branch allows the test to silently pass if `res` is `Ok(_)`. If ring capacity or completion queue behavior changes such that the 512 operations do not trigger completion dispatch during registration, `res.is_err()` will be false and the test will pass without actually verifying panic safety or slot retention. Explicitly asserting that `res.is_err()` ensures any failure to trigger the waker panic fails loudly.
